The Relative Strength Index (RSI) is holding just above the oversold zone, indicating that selling pressure may be easing. If the stock sustains above Rs 3,600, a rebound towards Rs 3,900 cannot be ruled out. However, a decisive breakdown below this support could weaken the technical structure. Given the favourable risk-reward setup near the support zone, traders may consider buying L&T with a stop-loss at Rs 3,550.
Birlasoft is showing signs of a potential bullish reversal, supported by the formation of a bullish divergence on the daily chart. This divergence indicates that the underlying selling pressure may be weakening, increasing the possibility of a recovery.
Following the divergence, the stock closed above its 10-day and 20-day Exponential Moving Averages (EMAs), accompanied by a significant surge in trading volumes. This combination suggests improving buying interest and strengthening bullish momentum.
Moreover, the 10-day and 20-day EMAs are now acting as support, indicating a possible role reversal in which previously challenging moving averages begin to support the price. Based on this technical setup, traders may consider buying Birlasoft in the Rs 300–310 range, with a stop-loss at Rs 270 on a closing basis.
